cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this analysis helps your work, cite this repository and the source datasets listed in REFERENCES.md."
type: software
title: "Hypothesis generation from public lung single-cell and multiome data"
authors:
  - family-names: "Xorca"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xorca0711/scRNA_seq"
url: "https://github.com/xorca0711/scRNA_seq"
abstract: >-
  An analysis log whose purpose is hypothesis generation from an integrative
  reanalysis of public lung single-cell and multiome data. Deposited count
  matrices are re-analysed with frameworks newer than the source papers, with
  the authors' annotations held out, to surface phenotypes and data
  distributions, within the theme of which epithelial and immune-state
  programmes distinguish productive lung repair from persistent remodelling
  after injury.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scanpy
  - lung repair
  - macrophage and monocyte states
  - lineage tracing
date-released: 2026-09-10
